hadiths[20]{hadithnumber,text}:
"671","Chapter 69: What has come concerning riba. 703 - Ziyad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the eater of riba, its feeder, its two witnesses, and its writer, and said: They are equal."
"672","704 - Ahmad ibn Yusuf al-Sulami and Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn Ma'bad narrated to us, they said: al-Nadr - that is Ibn Muhammad - narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah - meaning Ibn Ammar - narrated to us, from Yahya, he said: Abu Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Riba has seventy gates, the lightest of them with Allah is like one who marries his mother."
"673","705 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from 'Abdillah al-Za'farani, from Abu al-Mutawakkil, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Silver for silver and gold for gold, equal for equal; whoever gives more or takes more has committed riba; the taker and the giver are equal."
"674","706 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Men of knowledge informed me, among them Malik ibn Anas, that Nafi', the freedman of Ibn 'Umar, narrated to them, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not sell gold for gold except like for like, and do not give preference to some of it over some, and do not sell silver for silver except like for like, and do not give preference to some of it over some, and do not sell anything of it absent for present."
"675","707 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Khalid al-Hadh-dha', from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, from 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gold for gold, silver for silver, dates for dates, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, and salt for salt - like for like, hand to hand; but if these kinds differ, then sell as you wish, provided it is hand to hand."
"676","708 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Malik ibn Aws ibn al-Hadathan, he said: I heard 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gold for silver is riba except on the spot, and dates for dates is riba except on the spot, and wheat for wheat is riba except on the spot, and barley for barley is riba except on the spot."
"677","709 - Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Waki' narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Hakim ibn Jabir al-Ahmasi, from 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him. And Mahmud ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Marwan - meaning Ibn Mu'awiyah - narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Hakim ibn Jabir, from 'Ubadah ibn al-Samit, may Allah be pleased with him - and this is his hadith from Waki' - he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Gold for gold, pan for pan, and silver for silver, pan for pan, until he specified salt. 'Ubadah, may Allah be pleased with him, said: By Allah, I do not care not to be in the land of Mu'awiyah. And Marwan said: Until he specified mentioning salt."
"678","710 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Hisham informed us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: We used to be given inferior dates in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we would sell two sa's for one sa', so that was raised to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: No two sa's of dates for one sa', and no two dirhams for one dirham."
"679","711 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Abu Hani' al-Khawlani informed me that he heard 'Ulayy ibn Rabah al-Lakhmi saying: I heard Fadalah ibn 'Ubayd al-Ansari saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a necklace containing beads and gold while he was at Khaybar, and it was from the spoils being sold, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that the gold in the necklace be removed by itself, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Gold for gold, weight for weight."
"680","712 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: I used to sell camels at al-Baqi', so I would sell for dinars and take dirhams, and sell for dirhams and take dinars. He said: So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the house of Hafsah, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, wait a moment, I ask you! I sell camels at al-Baqi', and I sell for dinars and take dirhams, and sell for dirhams and take dinars. He said: There is no harm, if you take them at the rate of the day, as long as you do not part while anything remains between you."
"681","713 - Ibn al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of dates until their ripeness appears, and forbade the sale of fruit for fruit."
"682","714 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam narrated to us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Malik ibn Anas and Usamah ibn Zayd informed me, from 'Abdillah ibn Yazid, the freedman of al-Aswad ibn Sufyan, that Abu 'Ayyash, the freedman of Banu Zuhrah, informed him that Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to him, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) being asked about buying dates with fresh dates, and he said: Does the fresh date decrease when it dries? They said: Yes, so he forbade it."
"683","715 - 'Abdillah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from Zayd ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted 'araya to be sold by its estimate in measure."
"684","716 - Muhammad ibn 'Abdillah ibn 'Abd al-Hakam informed us that Ibn Wahb informed them, he said: Malik informed me, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, that Abu Sufyan, the freedman of Ibn Abi Ahmad, informed him, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the sale of 'araya for less than five awsuq, or in five awsuq. Dawud ibn al-Husayn doubted: he did not know whether five awsuq or less than five."
"685","717 - Ibrahim ibn 'Abdillah narrated to us, he said: Yazid - meaning Ibn Harun - informed us, he said: Yahya informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, he said: Zayd ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, informed me: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the 'ariyyah to be taken for its like by estimate as dates, which its people eat as fresh dates."
"686","718 - 'Abdillah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from 'Abdillah ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dealt with Khaybar for half of what comes out of it, of dates or crops."
"687","719 - Abu Sa'id al-Ashajj narrated to us, he said: 'Uqbah narrated to me, he said: 'Ubaydullah narrated to us, he said: Nafi' narrated to me, from Ibn 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dealt with the people of Khaybar for half of what comes out of it of crops or dates, and he used to give his wives every year one hundred wasqs, eighty wasqs of dates and twenty wasqs of barley. When 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, rose, he divided Khaybar, and gave the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the choice to have land allocated to them or to guarantee them the wasqs; some of them chose to have land allocated, and some chose the wasqs. And 'A'ishah and Hafsah, may Allah be pleased with them both, were among those who chose the wasqs."
"688","720 - Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said: Musa ibn 'Uqbah narrated to me, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, that 'Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, expelled the Jews from the land of the Hijaz; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he prevailed over Khaybar, wanted to expel the Jews from it, and the land when he prevailed over it belonged to Allah and to His Messenger and to the Muslims, and he wanted to expel the Jews from it, so the Jews asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to leave them in it on condition that they undertake its work, with half the dates for them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: We leave you in it on that as long as we wish. So they remained in it until 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, expelled them to Tayma' and Ariha'."
"689","721 - 'Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us, he said: 'Isa - meaning Ibn Yunus - informed us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from 'A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought food from a Jew and pawned to him an iron armor."
"690","722 - 'Abdillah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya - meaning Ibn Sa'id - narrated to us, from Zakariyya - meaning Ibn Abi Za'idah - from 'Amir, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A back is ridden in return for its upkeep when it is pawned, and the milk of a milch animal is drunk when it is pawned, and the upkeep is upon the one who drinks and rides."
